igh reasoning with retry on multi-hop and ambiguous-entity asks.", "settles": "Its pass rate and tail latency in each task, so it can be read against both gates like the configurations that ran."}, {"text": "Fix multi-hop decomposition and ambiguous-name clarification for Brisk-S low reasoning with retry, then rerun those two tasks with their case counts recorded.", "settles": "Whether a configuration already inside the budget can clear the pass-rate gate on its own."}, {"text": "The planner owner declares which line gives if no configuration or mix clears both: the latency budget or the pass-rate gate.", "settles": "Turns the diagnosis into a decision between Brisk-S high reasoning with retry and Brisk-S low reasoning with retry."}, {"text": "Rerun multi-hop for Brisk-S high reasoning with retry at about {assumed.share.settle.criteria.pass_rate.brisk-s.high.r1.task.multihop.cases_needed_two_sided} cases, assuming the task holds its traffic share today.", "settles": "Whether its thin multi-hop clearance holds, if it is taken forward."}], "method": [{"term": "Configurations", "text": "{n_candidates} configurations crossing three models, three reasoning levels and retry on or off; no control, so every comparison is between two configurations' own figures."}, {"term": "Cases", "text": "{scoreboard.brisk-s.high.r1.cases} cases per configuration, none lost, spread over four tasks by traffic share; per-task figures state no case count."}, {"term": "Pass", "text": "The campaign does not state its pass rule; the kept failures are scored against an expected call plan and classed as a missing call, wrong arguments or the wrong tool."}, {"term": "Gates", "text": "Pass rate at least {criteria.pass_rate.threshold} and tail latency at most {criteria.p95.threshold}, each read in every task on the point estimate."}, {"term": "Tail latency", "text": "The p95 latency, recorded only over all cases; the budget is declared per task, so it is read here as unknown in each task, with an ov